screen.LIGHTING=Lighting
screen.LIGHTING.comment=Sunlight and shadows, bounced light, and light from torches and other glowing blocks.
option.VOXEL_VOLUME_SIZE=Voxel Range
option.VOXEL_VOLUME_SIZE.comment=How far around you the world is copied into voxels for Global Illumination, block lighting and World-Space Reflections. Reaches half as far up and down. Global Illumination needs 128 blocks or less. §c[-]§r Higher values greatly decrease performance.
value.VOXEL_VOLUME_SIZE.128=64 Blocks
value.VOXEL_VOLUME_SIZE.192=96 Blocks
value.VOXEL_VOLUME_SIZE.256=128 Blocks
value.VOXEL_VOLUME_SIZE.384=192 Blocks
value.VOXEL_VOLUME_SIZE.512=256 Blocks

screen.GI_CONFIG=Indirect Lighting
screen.GI_CONFIG.comment=Light that bounces off surfaces, light from the sky, and how walls, roofs and corners block it.
option.GI=Global Illumination
option.GI.comment=Traces rays through a voxel copy of the world around you, so light bounces between surfaces and roofs and walls block sky light. Needs a Voxel Range of 128 blocks or less. §c[-]§r Greatly decreases performance.
option.GI_SCREEN_TRACE=Screen-Space Tracing
option.GI_SCREEN_TRACE.comment=Rays first check what is on screen for about one block before using the voxel world. Adds fine contact shading, lets players and mobs block and reflect light, and shades terrain beyond the Voxel Range.
option.GI_STRENGTH=GI Strength
option.GI_STRENGTH.comment=Brightness of the light Global Illumination traces: light bounced off surfaces and light from torches, lanterns and other glowing blocks. Sky light is not affected.
option.GI_SUN_BOUNCE=Sunlight Bounce
option.GI_SUN_BOUNCE.comment=How much sunlight and moonlight bounces off lit surfaces into nearby shade. Multiplies GI Strength for this light only. 0.00 turns it off.
option.GI_SKY_SHADOW=Sky Light Occlusion
option.GI_SKY_SHADOW.comment=How much roofs, walls and trees block light from the sky. Lower values keep indoor and shaded areas brighter.
option.GI_COLOR=Color Bleeding
option.GI_COLOR.comment=How strongly bounced light takes on the color of the surface it came from, such as a red tint next to a red wall. Brightness stays the same. 1.0 is realistic.
option.GI_MULTI_BOUNCE=Multiple Bounces
option.GI_MULTI_BOUNCE.comment=How much light keeps bouncing after the first bounce. Higher values brighten enclosed spaces. 0.00 is a single bounce.
option.AO_TYPE=Ambient Occlusion
option.AO_TYPE.comment=Darkens corners and creases. Only used while Global Illumination is off, which does this by itself. Vanilla AO is free, SSAO is fast, GTAO is the most accurate and the slowest.
value.AO_TYPE.0=Vanilla AO
value.AO_TYPE.1=SSAO
value.AO_TYPE.2=GTAO
option.AO_STRENGTH=AO Strength
option.AO_STRENGTH.comment=How dark Ambient Occlusion makes corners and creases. Only used while Global Illumination is off.

screen.GI_QUALITY_CONFIG=Quality & Performance
screen.GI_QUALITY_CONFIG.comment=Resolution, ray length and noise reduction for Global Illumination.
option.GI_RESOLUTION=Resolution
option.GI_RESOLUTION.comment=Resolution the rays are traced at. §c[-]§r Full traces four times as many pixels as Half.
value.GI_RESOLUTION.1=Full
value.GI_RESOLUTION.2=Half
value.GI_RESOLUTION.4=Quarter
option.GI_RAY_STEPS=Ray Length
option.GI_RAY_STEPS.comment=How far rays can travel through the voxel world. A ray that runs out counts as reaching open sky. §c[-]§r Higher values decrease performance.
option.GI_ACCUMULATION=Smoothing Time
option.GI_ACCUMULATION.comment=Seconds of past frames blended into the result. Higher values are smoother and less noisy, but lighting reacts slower to changes such as a torch being placed.
suffix.GI_ACCUMULATION=s
option.GI_FILTER=Denoiser Strength
option.GI_FILTER.comment=How much the result is blurred to hide noise. 0.00 turns it off.
option.GI_LEAF_PASS=Light Through Leaves
option.GI_LEAF_PASS.comment=How much light passes through leaves. 0.00 makes leaves fully solid.
option.GI_RAY_RATE=Ray Rate
option.GI_RAY_RATE.comment=How often pixels with a settled result trace a new ray. Half and Quarter skip frames in a rotating tile pattern, which is faster. §c[-]§r At lower rates settled lighting reacts slower to changes.
value.GI_RAY_RATE.1=Full
value.GI_RAY_RATE.2=Half
value.GI_RAY_RATE.4=Quarter
option.GI_REUSE=Sample Reuse
option.GI_REUSE.comment=Pixels share the light they found with their neighbours and keep aiming at it, which removes most of the grain without extra blur. §c[-]§r Slightly decreases performance.
option.GI_CACHE_RANGE=Irradiance Cache Range
option.GI_CACHE_RANGE.comment=Share of the Voxel Range around you where the irradiance cache traces more rays every frame. Inside it, bounce light is smoother and lighting changes such as a torch being removed show up sooner. Off keeps the slower update everywhere. §c[-]§r Higher values decrease performance.
value.GI_CACHE_RANGE.0.00=Off
value.GI_CACHE_RANGE.0.10=10%
value.GI_CACHE_RANGE.0.20=20%
value.GI_CACHE_RANGE.0.30=30%
value.GI_CACHE_RANGE.0.40=40%
value.GI_CACHE_RANGE.0.50=50%
value.GI_CACHE_RANGE.0.75=75%
value.GI_CACHE_RANGE.1.00=100%
